{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyConjecture","@type":"LeanModule","name":"FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyConjecture","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.CrossProduct","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Deriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.ExpDeriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt"],"declarations":29,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.levi_nondegenerate_somewhere_of_blowup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.levi_nondegenerate_somewhere_of_blowup","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L245-L260","doc":"What branch (B) gives, stated as a derivation: under the carrier, a blowing-up\nsolution has a non-zero Levi scalar somewhere in every high-vorticity set.  This\nis the contrapositive of the carrier's field and adds nothing to it; it is here\nso that the shape of the claim is visible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.LeviDegeneracy.degenerate_implies_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.LeviDegeneracy.degenerate_implies_regular","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L242-L242","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.LeviDegeneracy.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.LeviDegeneracy.mk","kind":"ctor","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L240-L240","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.LeviDegeneracy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.LeviDegeneracy","kind":"class","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L230-L243","doc":"**`conj:levi-degeneracy`, branch (B), re-scoped (open; no instance).**\n\nOn every solution in the caller's class, if the Levi scalar `ξ·curl ξ` vanishes\non the high-vorticity set then the vorticity stays bounded up to `T*`.\n\nNo standard result supplies this.  The Beirão da Veiga–Berselli hypothesis\nbounds all of `∇ξ` from above on the high-vorticity set, and the vanishing of\nthe one component `ξ·curl ξ` does not imply it — nor does its non-vanishing\n(`beltrami_refutes_branchA` is the other side of that).  This is a primary\nconjecture; assuming it is assuming the open content. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:levi-degeneracy","label":"conj:levi-degeneracy","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.blowup_forces_direction_incoherence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.blowup_forces_direction_incoherence","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L208-L226","doc":"**Blow-up forces direction incoherence** (the true conditional statement;\ncontrapositive of Beirão da Veiga–Berselli).  If a solution blows up at `T*`,\nthen for every threshold `Ω > 0` and constant `C ≥ 0` there is a time `t < T*` and\ntwo high-vorticity points at which the line field violates the ½-Hölder bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.BeiraoDaVeigaBerselliCriterion.criterion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.BeiraoDaVeigaBerselliCriterion.criterion","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L205-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.BeiraoDaVeigaBerselliCriterion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.BeiraoDaVeigaBerselliCriterion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L202-L202","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.BeiraoDaVeigaBerselliCriterion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.BeiraoDaVeigaBerselliCriterion","kind":"class","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L191-L206","doc":"**The Beirão da Veiga–Berselli criterion, as a cited hypothesis.**\n\n`IsSolution s` is the caller's predicate \"`s` is a smooth solution of unforced\nNavier–Stokes on `[0, T*)`, in the class of the theorem, with `curlDir` the curl\nof `dir`\".  The single field is the published theorem: on such a solution, the\n½-Hölder direction condition on the high-vorticity set prevents blow-up.  It is a\n**hypothesis**, never discharged here.  The class carries the theorem, not the\nconclusion derived from it below.\n\nBibliographic data confirmed via secondary sources; the primary text is not held\n(`docs/audits/2026-10-12-ns-v1-geometric-depletion.md` §1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.LeviDegenerateOnHighVort","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.LeviDegenerateOnHighVort","kind":"def","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L183-L187","doc":"**Levi degeneracy on the high-vorticity set**: `ξ·curl ξ = 0` wherever\n`|ω| > Ω`, for some `Ω > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.VorticityBounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.VorticityBounded","kind":"def","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L178-L181","doc":"**No blow-up at `T*`**, in Beale–Kato–Majda form: `|ω|` bounded on\n`[0, T*) × ℝ³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.DirectionHalfHolder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.DirectionHalfHolder","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L170-L176","doc":"**The Beirão da Veiga–Berselli hypothesis**: `|sin φ| ≤ C |x − y|^{1/2}` on\nthe high-vorticity set, written squared: `|ξ(x) × ξ(y)|² ≤ C²·|x − y|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.HighVort","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.HighVort","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L166-L168","doc":"`(t, x)` lies in the high-vorticity set `|ω| > Ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.IsVorticityDirection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.IsVorticityDirection","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L161-L164","doc":"`ξ = ω/|ω|` wherever `ω ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.curlDir","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.curlDir","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L157-L157","doc":"The value of `curl ξ` at `(t, x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.dir","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.dir","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L155-L155","doc":"Direction field `ξ(t, x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.vort","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.vort","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L153-L153","doc":"Vorticity `ω(t, x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.Tstar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.Tstar","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L151-L151","doc":"Blow-up time candidate `T*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L149-L149","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.FlowData","kind":"structure","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L145-L157","doc":"Data of a flow on `[0, T*)` in `ℝ³` coordinates: the vorticity `ω(t, x)`,\nthe direction field `ξ(t, x)` and the value `curl ξ (t, x)`.  **Data only**: the\nrelations between the fields are named propositions below, and solution-hood is a\npredicate the caller supplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltrami_refutes_branchA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltrami_refutes_branchA","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L132-L141","doc":"**Branch (A) fails for this flow** ([`conj:levi-degeneracy`], scope (b) for\nthe implication under `Θ = f·ξ♭`): the Levi scalar is `1` everywhere — never\ndegenerate — and the vorticity stays bounded for all `t ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltrami_vorticity_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltrami_vorticity_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L121-L130","doc":"**Bounded vorticity for all time**: `|ω|² = e^{-2νt}·|ξ|² ≤ 1` for `ν, t ≥ 0`\n(here `ω = curl u = u`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltrami_heat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltrami_heat","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L109-L119","doc":"**Heat equation, componentwise.**  For `u = e^{-νt}(sin z, cos z, 0)`:\n`∂_t u_i = ν ∂_z² u_i` for `i = 1, 2` (the third component is `0`).  With\n`div u = 0`, `(u·∇)u = 0` and `p ≡ 0` (file docstring) this is the unforced\nNavier–Stokes system. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltrami_second_deriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltrami_second_deriv","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L100-L107","doc":"Spatial factor: `∂_z² sin = -sin` and `∂_z² cos = -cos`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.decay_deriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.decay_deriv","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L93-L98","doc":"Temporal factor `e^{-νt}` solves `g' = -ν g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltrami_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltrami_unit","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L88-L91","doc":"`ξ` is a unit field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltrami_levi_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltrami_levi_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L79-L86","doc":"**The Levi scalar is identically `1`**: `ξ·curl ξ = sin² z + cos² z = 1`.\nSo `ker ξ♭` is a contact structure on all of `T³`, with a constant,\nnon-degenerate Levi datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltrami_curl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltrami_curl","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L75-L77","doc":"**`curl ξ = ξ`** for the Beltrami direction field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.curlZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.curlZ","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L70-L73","doc":"`curl` of a field `(a(z), b(z), 0)` depending on `z` only:\n`(-b'(z), a'(z), 0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltramiDir","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviDegeneracyQ1.beltramiDir","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/levi-degeneracy-conjecture.lean#L67-L68","doc":"The Beltrami direction field `ξ(z) = (sin z, cos z, 0)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}